<title>USA: Conrail sees traffic boosting income.</title>
<headline>Conrail sees traffic boosting income.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Increased freight traffic will account for about $200 million in the projected $550 million in annual benefits from the proposed merger of Conrail Inc and CSX Corp, Conrail Chairman David LeVan said.</p>
<p>LeVan told a telephone news conference that no price increases were projected in the analysis. Other benefits would come from cost savings and rationalizations, the two companies said in announcing the merger.</p>
<p>CSX Chairman John Snow said there would be an initial attrition of jobs in the combined firm. But over the long run the merger is a &quot;growth story,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
